<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65982" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μελητίδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, prov. at Athens for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a blockhead</i> (in form a patronymic from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλητος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				991
			</span></i> (lyr., prob.), <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				53
			</span></i>, etc.—In codd. usu. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μελιτίδης</span>: hence derived by Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> l. c. and <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1735.51
			</span></i> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλι</span>, though second
			syll. is long.</div>
